WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
This is Holderness, on the North
Sea coast of East Yorkshire.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.230
Its cliffs are glacial
till: soft boulder clay,

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.690
about 20 metres high at Aldbrough.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.130
On average, they retreat between
1 and 4.5 metres every year.

5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.310
Year after year, more of this
coast falls into the sea.

6
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.430
So where did all that land go?

7
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.630
Was it lost far out at sea?

8
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.470
Did it simply dissolve?

9
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.910
In this mission, you'll find out why the
chalk of Flamborough Head stands firm

10
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.650
while the clay cliffs slump.

11
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.530
Then you'll build the
landforms waves carve,

12
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.910
from sea caves to stacks.

13
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: find out where
Holderness's lost land has gone.
